  "body": "Add a global sheet cut-order tree, hold-down sequencing, and cut-side planner in `crates/geometry/src/nesting/` (reusing the nesting rules from `crates/motion/src/plasma/nest.rs`).\n\nDepends on #2158 and #1861.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build one global containment forest across all closed contours and open chains on a nested sheet.\n- Assign each open chain to its smallest enclosing closed contour, or mark it top-level when outside all parts.\n- Assign each contour and chain a resolved cut role and cut side:\n  - Closed loops: `Outside`, `OnLine`, or `Inside` (`Auto` sets outer part outlines to `Outside`, holes to `Inside`, and islands inside holes to `Outside`).\n  - Open chains: `OnLine`, `Left`, or `Right`.\n  - Refuse `Inside` or `Outside` on an open chain by name.\n- Traverse the global containment tree in deterministic iterative post-order:\n  - Cut internal holes, pockets, and open features of a part before its outer outline.\n  - Cut small parts nested inside a hole before the enclosing hole cuts free.\n  - Order sibling parts at the same depth by increasing area (small parts before large parts) to preserve router vacuum hold-down and sheet rigidity.\n  - Reserve ordered pass phases: marking/scribe passes (`#1447`) first, internal/pocket passes next, rough/onion-skin profile passes next, and final onion-skin breakthrough passes last.\n- Compute minimum inside-corner cutter-radius clearance diagnostics when a circular tool (`radius = cut_width / 2`) cannot reach sharp concave corners.\n- Validate that no contour cuts after an enclosing contour has already freed its material.\n\n## Done means\n\nTests in `crates/geometry` verify inside-out cut order across a multi-part sheet containing nested holes, internal open cuts, and a small part placed inside a large hole, verify phase ordering for marking and onion-skin passes, confirm smaller sibling parts precede larger ones deterministically, report concave inside-corner radius limits, and refuse invalid open-chain side requests by name.\n\nPart of #2156\n",
